title: Start
tags:
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorId: 2
position: 0,0
---
This lesson is about the "action" statement, which couples a client-side event to a line of dialogue. Every action has a type and a value.

[[Show me a link.|Link]]
===
title: Link
tags:
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorId: 0
position: 320,0
---
An action of type "link" points at a URL.

<<action type="link" value="https://www.dialoguebranch.com/">>

[[Show me image and video.|Media]]
===
title: Media
tags:
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorId: 0
position: 640,0
---
The "image" and "video" types point at a resource.

<<action type="image" value="dog.png">>
<<action type="video" value="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ">>

[[Show me a generic action.|Generic]]
===
title: Generic
tags:
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorId: 0
position: 960,0
---
A "generic" action carries whatever your client wants to handle, plus any extra parameters.

<<action type="generic" value="OPEN_RECIPE_BOOK" delay="2000" page="42">>

[[Can an action sit in a reply?|Reply]]
===
title: Reply
tags:
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorId: 0
position: 1280,0
---
Yes. An action can also hang off a reply, and a link action can carry display text.

[[Open the book, please.|End|<<action type="generic" value="OPEN_RECIPE_BOOK">>]]
[[Visit the website.|End|<<action type="link" value="https://www.dialoguebranch.com/" text="website">>]]
===
title: End
tags:
speaker:
colorId: 5
position: 800,220
---

